sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor User as User or trigger
    participant HTTP as Function HTTP API
    participant Entity as Session Entity
    participant DTS as DTS session orchestrator
    participant Control as Short controller activities
    participant ACA as Customer ACA Sandbox
    participant Model as Authorized model endpoint
    participant Tools as External tools / MCP
    participant Blob as Customer Blob content

    Note over HTTP,Blob: Proposed / design discussion - not implemented or approved production architecture.
    Note over Control,ACA: Tables whole-agent execution is reuse evidence - the Durable bridge is new integration.
    Note over ACA,Blob: All ACA Sandbox Groups are customer-provided/customer-owned, NOT platform-owned.
    User->>HTTP: Start durable session run
    HTTP->>Blob: Persist owner-scoped immutable request
    HTTP->>DTS: Start / rejoin orchestration with refs only
    HTTP-->>User: 202 + tracking URL (not admission or final success)
    DTS->>Entity: Admit owner + agent + session + request
    Entity-->>DTS: Admitted generation fence + binding / committed refs
    Note over Entity,DTS: Entity owns admission, generation, cancellation and refs, not transcripts/files.<br/>DTS owns explicit control flow - its history carries bounded metadata, not content.
    DTS->>Control: Start or adopt attempt (stable id + fence)
    Control->>ACA: Idempotent start/adopt, ordinary agent.run() only for new attempt
    ACA-->>Control: Attempt handle, execution continues remotely
    Control-->>DTS: Same attempt ref
    Note over DTS,Control: Short bounded activities return promptly - polls never call agent.run() or park a worker.
    par Opaque run inside ACA
        loop Agent-internal model / tool work until attempt exits
            ACA->>Model: Model request using guest model authority
            Model-->>ACA: Answer / tool calls
            ACA->>ACA: Local tool + workspace operations
            ACA->>Tools: External tool / MCP call (if used)
            Tools-->>ACA: Result / receipt if supported
        end
        Note over ACA,Tools: Unlike Durable Agent Loop, internal model/tool calls are NOT separate DTS checkpoints.<br/>Model authority may be shared with tool code - no brain/tool least-privilege separation promised.
    and Durable supervision of the same attempt
        loop While active, stop for terminal status or cancellation
            DTS->>DTS: Durable timer to next bounded poll / capture request
            DTS->>Control: Poll same attempt status (never restart)
            Control->>ACA: Bounded status + candidate lookup
            ACA-->>Control: Running / terminal / unavailable + refs
            Control-->>DTS: Status + bounded refs
            opt Still active, checkpoint request due (approximately 60 seconds, TBD)
                DTS->>Control: Request / inspect periodic checkpoint candidate
                Control->>ACA: Request candidate capture, bounded return, protocol TBD
                ACA-->>Control: Candidate handle or pending / unavailable
                Note over Control,Blob: Need consistent conversation/reasoning + workspace content + effect frontier/receipts.<br/>Safe capture, consistency and resume protocol are TBD - requested/raw is NOT committed.
                alt Candidate validated under a qualified protocol (TBD)
                    Control->>Blob: Persist validated candidate with controller-scoped permissions
                    Blob-->>Control: Immutable content refs + integrity hashes
                    Control-->>DTS: Candidate refs, NOT yet a recovery commit
                    DTS->>Entity: Conditional checkpoint commit (generation + attempt fence)
                    Entity-->>DTS: Accepted receipt => authoritative, rejected => retain prior ref
                else Missing / pending / inconsistent / unverified
                    Control-->>DTS: No advance to committed recovery state
                end
            end
            opt Controller restart or ACA backing loss
                DTS->>Control: Locate / adopt same live attempt if available
                Control->>Blob: If not live, read only qualified committed checkpoint
                Note over Control,ACA: Recovery requires supported restore + external-effect reconciliation (TBD).<br/>No usable checkpoint or unknown effects => fail / reconciliation required, never blind restart.
                Control->>ACA: Adopt live attempt, or restore/resume ONLY if recovery qualified
            end
        end
    end
    Note over ACA,Blob: ACA Disk preserves files, not executor memory. DTS/timers do not snapshot a Python stack.<br/>No exactly-once guarantee for arbitrary external effects.
    Note over Control,Blob: Customer Blob is recoverable transcript/workspace authority - persistence/commit is controller-mediated.<br/>No implicit broad guest permissions to Blob, Entity or DTS.
    alt Terminal success candidate
        DTS->>Control: Obtain final result and final content (bounded)
        Control->>ACA: Read terminal response + conversation/workspace + effect receipts
        ACA-->>Control: Final content (bounded refs / transfer)
        Control->>Blob: Persist and integrity-check final content
        Blob-->>Control: Verified final refs or persistence failure
        Control-->>DTS: Verified final refs or error
        DTS->>Entity: If persisted, fenced idempotent final commit + next generation
        Entity-->>DTS: Commit receipt or rejection (when attempted)
        alt Final content persisted and final commit accepted
            DTS-->>HTTP: Committed success + response ref
            HTTP->>Blob: Read owner-authorized, integrity-checked final response
            Blob-->>HTTP: Final response
            HTTP-->>User: Final result through tracking/result API
        else Persistence / commit incomplete or rejected
            DTS->>Entity: Record non-success without advancing recovery state
            DTS-->>HTTP: Non-success / recovery pending, no final success
            HTTP-->>User: Explicit status, not a successful answer
        end
    else Failed / cancelled / reconciliation required
        DTS->>Entity: Record cancellation / failure fence and explicit outcome
        DTS->>Control: Cancel / stop same attempt if needed (bounded)
        Control->>ACA: Best-effort cancel / stop, no new run
        Note over Entity,ACA: Cancellation is not proof effects stopped - unresolved effects need reconciliation.
        DTS-->>HTTP: Failed / cancelled / reconciliation required
        HTTP-->>User: Explicit non-success outcome
    end
